        "original_id": "4d7bb9c0-d885-55ad-997c-1b111478bda4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Panicum, Populus, Echinochloa colona\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy, geographic distribution\n\nFacts:\n- Panicum is a large genus of about 450 grass species native throughout the tropical regions of the world, with a few species extending into the northern temperate zone.\n- Populus is a genus of 25–35 species of deciduous flowering plants in the family Salicaceae that is native to most of the Northern Hemisphere.\n- Echinochloa colona was formerly classified as a species of Panicum.",
